# Browser verification (SDET-58)

**One line:** Confirm **behaviour**, not just appearance.

## When this rule applies

Work that touches user-visible Demo Shop behaviour: page objects, components, UI tests, or files under `src/main/resources/demo-app/`.

## Layout or structure changed — walk like a real user

If the change affects **layout, navigation, forms, or visible copy** (including `demo-app` HTML, header/cart, new screen, or locators tied to moved elements):

1. Use **browser tools** (`cursor-ide-browser`): open the app (Demo Shop URL from config / `@BeforeSuite` setup).
2. **Exercise the flow end-to-end** — navigate, click, type, submit — the same path the test or user story describes.
3. Check **success and failure paths** the change touches (empty field, invalid login, error banner, etc.), not only the happy path.
4. **Desktop vs mobile:** only compare both if the ticket or change explicitly affects responsive layout; otherwise desktop is enough.

A **single screenshot without interaction is not verification.**

## Smaller changes (proportional)

Locator-only or one-line page fix with **no layout change:** re-run the **smallest relevant test** (one method or one class), not a full manual regression.

## After `/new-page` or `/new-test`

Before calling the work done:

- Browser walk of the affected journey **or**
- Run smoke as the minimum automated check (see below).

## No browser tools in this session

Say so explicitly. Substitute:

```bash
./mvnw test -DsuiteXmlFile=src/test/resources/suites/smoke.xml
```

(Use `regression.xml` only when the change is regression-scoped and smoke does not cover it.)

Report pass/fail from Surefire — smoke is the substitute, not a skip.

## Do not

- Treat one static screenshot as “verified UI.”
- Run full manual regression for a tiny, isolated locator tweak.
